    <string name="faq_ans_1">"If this app doesn't work correctly or can't force stop apps, please do the following things:

1. Make sure that Shizuku is running.
2. Exit AppSleep properly and reopen it.

If this doesn't work, then email us with your problem. We will do our best to fix that issue ASAP."</string>
    <string name="faq_ans_2">Force-stopping apps directly are not possible without system API. Shizuku provides something like being a <b>middle man</b> to receive requests from the app, send them to the system server, and send back the results.</string>
    <string name="faq_ans_3">"Whitelist is the app list where you can add your sensitive apps like antivirus, music player etc.

These apps will be ignored during the force stop operation"</string>
    <string name="faq_ans_4">"No, you needn't. Purchase status saves on your Google Play address. So, if you use the same Gmail address on your new phone, you needn't purchase it again. Just download AppSleep from Google Play using the same Gmail address. Open AppSleep and click the "<b>UPGRADE</b> button and restore your purchase.</string>
    <string name="faq_ans_5">"If the premium version is lost and the app doesn't detect your purchase anymore, do the following things:
➨ Click the "<b>UPGRADE</b>" button from settings.
➨ Click the "<b>Restore Purchase</b> button.</string>
